  <static seed="2110" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/FractionPercentDecimal/DecimalToFraction40.pg">
    <statement><p>Write the decimal number as a fraction.</p>
<p><m>0.654</m> = <fillin characters="11" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>{\frac{327}{500}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><m>0.654</m> is read as 654 thousandths, so it can be written as <m>\frac{654}{1000}</m>, which can be reduced to <m>{{\frac{327}{500}}}</m> by dividing <m>2</m> in both the numerator and denominator.</p>
</solution>
